  "prompt": "Is a ₱14,000 monthly residential unit rental subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "bd19b3d7a220132a618a3777a33fdfa0b34099ea",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nIs a ₱14,000 monthly residential unit rental subject to VAT?\n\n### Short Answer\nNo, a ₱14,000 monthly residential unit rental is not subject to VAT.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, landlords renting out residential units for ₱14,000 per month should not charge VAT on the rental payments. They should ensure that their lease agreements reflect this exemption to avoid any potential tax liabilities. It is advisable for landlords to maintain proper documentation to support the VAT-exempt status of their rental income in case of any inquiries from the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
